===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|medicine|cytology}} A [[primal]] [[undifferentiated]] cell from which a [[variety]] of other cells can [[develop]] through the [[process]] of [[cellular]] [[differentiation]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2002|author=Haifan Lin|chapter=The stem-cell niche theory: Lessons from flies,|title=Nature Reviews: Genetics|volume=3|page=931
|passage='''Stem cells''' are characterized by their ability to self-renew and to produce numerous differentiated cell types, and are directly responsible for generating and maintaining tissues and organs.}}

